// Level 1 - Village Outskirts (hospital interior), collision grid for map.png
//
// GENERATED by tools/MaskToMap.java from a hand-cleaned reference image (a
// polished export of tools/VisualizeCollision.java's overlay, red = blocked,
// everything else = walkable) - do not hand-edit the grid below; regenerate
// from an updated reference image instead. The art's grid is 41.2667 px per
// tile with its origin at image pixel (32, 32), giving 45 x 33 tiles over the
// content box (x 32..1888, y 32..1394). GameScreen scales map.png to match
// those numbers.
//
// RESOLUTION: rows below are COLLISION CELLS, three per tile edge, so this file
// is 135 x 99. Collision is tested per cell; gameplay (contamination cloud BFS,
// tile indices on the wire) still works in whole 45 x 33 tiles. The finer grid
// exists because the art is hand-drawn and its walls do not sit on the tile
// grid - at tile resolution collision either ate walkable corridor or let
// players clip into walls.
//
// Rows read top-down as in the image; TileMap.fromRows flips them so world y=0
// is the BOTTOM row. '#' = blocked, '.' = walkable.
//
// FLOOR: every room and corridor is floored with the same cool blue-grey tile.
// The warm beige bands are wall faces drawn in perspective (they carry the room
// signs) and the warm greys beneath them are furniture. Do not widen isFloor to
// accept warm pixels to "open up" a room - a wall face, a door leaf, a bed frame
// and a sign plaque are all the same beige, so every threshold loose enough to
// catch one lets players walk on counters and wall tops.
//
// DOORWAYS: drawn doors are not floor-coloured, so they classify as wall. Two
// mechanisms open them:
//  1. the connectivity pass, which guarantees no room is sealed off, and
//  2. GenMap.FORCED_DOORS, a hand-written list for doors players actually walk
//     up to. Mechanism 1 only opens a route when a room is OTHERWISE unreachable,
//     so a room reachable the long way round keeps its visible door shut - which
//     is exactly what players bump into. Add to that list when you find one.
//
// Openings are widened to a full tile deliberately: the player's collision radius
// is 0.25 tiles (0.75 cells), so a gap under ~1.5 cells is connected on paper but
// impossible to walk through. LevelLoaderTest asserts reachability in ERODED
// space (where the player's disc actually fits) using CollisionSystem itself, so
// sealing a room here fails the build rather than the playtest.
//
// subdivisions: 3
